A||N||2||FieroFanaticus2||Quarter Panel Trim Removal -- please help||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||08-19-2001||09:41 PM||||Ok, so I've had these side scoops for several months yet and all they are doing is sitting around collecting dust.  I need to know how to remove the trim (the black plastic piece) that is on the quarter panels so I can get them off and get the scoops cut and drilled to fit.  I tried once before but couldn't figure it out and didn't want to break anything.  Does someone have a solution?  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||MrPBody||08-19-2001||09:54 PM||||As I recall --<P>One fastener in the door jamb; depending on the year, it screws out or pulls out.<P>One fastener in the fender well?  Maybe one of the screws that holds fender liner.<P>Then pry off the molding strip.  You may break some molding clips.  Fiero Store sells replacements.<P>This is only the beginning if you want to remove the quarter panel.  You have to remove the rocker panel, drill out rivets, and other fun stuff.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroFanaticus2||08-20-2001||05:31 PM||||Yeah, I know, sounds like a real blast.  Drilling out the rivets and removing the rockers is not a problem, I just can't figure how to get the black trim pieces off without breaking them.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dump_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
